    "196": "Page 196. The hospital ship Centaur. IMAGINED Written for this case, based on real events, not a real document. A desk in an archive. Late. Today Real photograph: the hospital ship Centaur, Sydney, 1943. Australian War Memorial 302800. Photographer not identified. Copyright expired, public domain. The lamp makes a small circle on the desk. The rest of the room can wait. A folder sits where the last reader left it. No name on the cover. Only a ship, and a date: May 1943. The journalist does not start with a theory. They start with what is in front of them. The first slip is a telegram. A stamp on it says Reconstruction. It is not a real telegram, and it is not addressed to a real family. The wording is still the kind of wording that arrived at a door. Reopen the Record: Australian Histories · sample · 152",
